\ port/gforth/kernel.4 - relf's kernel words that relfsh uses and gforth
\ lacks, or has under another meaning; loaded after sys.fs, before the port.

BASE @  DECIMAL

\ Names are case-sensitive in relf and not in gforth, where the shell's
\ CMD-OPT-v and CMD-OPT-V were one word - `command -v` described as -V
\ does. So the port and the shell are defined in a table, gforth's
\ case-sensitive word list, on top of the search order, with gforth's own
\ words below it; FORTH-WORDLIST is that table to the shell, whose MAIN
\ puts it on top (tree.4) and makes it CURRENT, as relf's forth word list
\ is for words a forth command defines. boot.4 sets the order up again.
table CONSTANT RELF-WORDLIST
RELF-WORDLIST >order  definitions
: FORTH-WORDLIST ( --- wid )  RELF-WORDLIST ;

\ START: relf's dictionary base, which relf adds to an offset kept in the
\ image (@XT, ROOT-WORDLIST). gforth's image loads where it was saved, so
\ the offsets are the addresses themselves.
VARIABLE START   0 START !

\ SID SRC #SRC: relf's input source, which a THROW out of its EVALUATE does
\ not restore, so the shell keeps them around each builtin (RUN-CAUGHT).
\ gforth's EVALUATE restores its own on a THROW; these only have to exist.
VARIABLE SID   VARIABLE SRC   VARIABLE #SRC

\ MAIN sets relf's search order to FORTH FORTH and the include buffer's
\ pointer back (tree.4). gforth's FORTH-WORDLIST, CONTEXT (the order's
\ top) and CURRENT take that as meant; #ORDER and the buffer have only to
\ exist - gforth's order is one deep at boot, and its includes are its own.
VARIABLE #ORDER
CREATE INCLUDE-BUFFER 512 ALLOT   VARIABLE INCLUDE-POINTER

\ kernel.4's, which gforth lacks
: CELL- ( a-addr1 --- a-addr2 )  1 CELLS - ;

\ The data stack's depth in cells, gforth's -d: by gforth's ENVIRONMENT?,
\ which port/relf.4 replaces with extend.4's (it answers nothing).
: STACK-CELLS ( --- n )  S" STACK-CELLS" ENVIRONMENT? 0= IF 2048 THEN ;

\ S0 and R0: the stacks' bases. The shell gives a forth command a stack of
\ its own by setting S0 (DO-FORTH), so that DEPTH counts from there -
\ gforth's DEPTH counts from sp0, so S0 is sp0.
: S0 ( --- a-addr )  sp0 ;
: R0 ( --- a-addr )  rp0 ;

BASE !
